{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1483135-cross-overs-in-revised-v20","id":1483135,"title":"Cross Overs in Revised/V20","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2022-06-05T09:20:53-07:00","id":1483135,"title":"Cross Overs in Revised/V20","content":"What has been your experience with Crossovers in Vampire? Personally, I think as an &quot;Oh Shit&quot; factor it's not bad, but familiarity breeds contempt if done too much. <br /> <br /> Which ones are too over powered or under powered against vampires, do you think?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27252-hades","name":"Hades","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"110"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-05T09:26:12-07:00","id":1483137,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hades</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1483135-cross-overs-in-revised-v20#post1483135\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What has been your experience with Crossovers in Vampire? Personally, I think as an &quot;Oh Shit&quot; factor it's not bad, but familiarity breeds contempt if done too much.<br /> <br /> Which ones are too over powered or under powered against vampires, do you think?</div> </div> </div> </div>To be perfectly honest, ALL of the cross over games I was in were utterly awful, the old world of darkness lines wasn't balanced against each other and the other splats were all more powerful and versatile than vampires, I ended up just tagging along while the mages (predictably), the werewolves and the freaking changelings handled everything, vampire characters are simply redundant and underpowered compared to the rest of the splats.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":27142,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27142-newb95","user":"Newb95","date":". 06-05-2022, 07:21 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27142-newb95","name":"Newb95","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"502"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-05T09:42:13-07:00","id":1483141,"title":"","content":"What do you mean by crossovers? Do you mean PCs being from the different game lines? If so, it's generally been bad. I have a great core group of players now so it's not an issue of having power gamers or the mechanics being disruptive. It's about preserving the feel of how the setting should be interpreted by each type of creature. It's hard to do justice for each kind with the limited time an ST has to spend on each PC.<br /> <br /> Or do you mean the ST actively including elements of the various game lines in his setting for one of the games? If so, I've had good success here. It's something I actively do now. Since I don't have to showcase the world, just a selected element of it, I can do so in a way that adds to the setting's feel instead of being disruptive to it. Now, that's usually something more of a sandbox element than through active plot I am running. So it only happens if one of the PCs decides to involve herself with an aspect of the sandbox.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-05T10:30:59-07:00","id":1483153,"title":"","content":"All of them. Each splat has their own advantages and such. Even so, every splat can dip their toes into the territory of the other splats to some extent. Since vampire's are best at social/political manipulation, which is seen as the weakest aspect in a crossover, you can see the first issue. The only splat that doesn't beat the vampire is the wraith, which is basically out because they're stuck in the shadowlands.<br /> <br /> The best advantage of the common kindred is their blood itself. They can half all bashing damage, completely bind people who taste their blood, and increase their physical attributes all the way to 10 in short bursts. That said, every other splat can do all these too, or come pretty close to replicating them with their abilities. As such, vampires are often seen as weaker thanks to this fact.<br /> <br /> That said, almost none of the splats know that much about each other. Mages surprisingly know little about the other splats due to never interacting that often. Werewolves only see vampires are wyrm tainted, and often nothing of the others. Changelings actively avoid the boring other splats. You get the idea. Outside of a few individual members of each splat, nobody knows much, if anything, about the other splats really.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><div align=\"left\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/7.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26764-vilenecromancer","name":"Vilenecromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26764_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"247"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-05T13:39:12-07:00","id":1483170,"title":"","content":"Cross Over or Kitchen Sink games are only as over or under powered as the game group want it to be.<br /> <br /> A Wraith cross over just makes the Necromancy clans/bloodlines have more depth and story hooks. But it can have the side issue of increasing the necromancers power over other clans.<br /> <br /> Adding Mage to Vampire usually breaks the game because of &quot;instant sunlight&quot; or the ever popular &quot;turn the vampire back into a human&quot; which tends to deflate the power of older vampires. Oddly enough I don't recall ever seeing a Mage sphere combination for increasing the power of a vampire.<br /> <br /> Though if you want truely game breaking, do a cross over with Exalted since its original concept was the true prehistory setting of WoD. Caine would probably classify as an Abyssal Half Caste locked at Essence 3, which means most vampires are barely essence 1. Now add an Essence 10 exalt into the setting and watch everything go horribly wrong.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/727-thoth","name":"Thoth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar727_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1689"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-05T14:03:06-07:00","id":1483171,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thoth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1483135-cross-overs-in-revised-v20?p=1483170#post1483170\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oddly enough I don't recall ever seeing a Mage sphere combination for increasing the power of a vampire.</div> </div> </div> </div>Someone make this a thread! We need this specifically!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><div align=\"left\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/7.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26764-vilenecromancer","name":"Vilenecromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26764_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"247"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-05T14:22:23-07:00","id":1483173,"title":"","content":"I don\u2019t like crossovers. In fact, for me, each game line exists as it\u2019s own world. Kindred from V:tM don\u2019t exist in the same universe as Garou from W:tA.<br /> <br /> The game lines aren\u2019t balanced with each other at all, but balance can be fixed with tweaking. The bigger issue is that the games are all thematically different and each setting has background setting features which are mutually exclusive with the games.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1129-sergeant-brother","name":"Sergeant Brother","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1129_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-05T14:28:37-07:00","id":1483174,"title":"","content":"My reference was to the PC's playing Vampires, and NPC's as the other splats. Im mostly familiar with Vampire, Mage and Demon, with Werewolf less so. Thus far, I've found Vampires to be on relatively equal footing with other splats of similar build (Werewolf does start much stronger but doesn't scale well against Vampires, Mages scale from equal footing to &quot;Jesus Christ, 12 Aggravated?&quot; relatively quickly but are quite the glass cannon, and Demons only scale well with xp purchased Apocalyptic Forms). <br /> <br /> That said, I have tweaked how Celerity, Fortitude and Defense (a stat that subtracts dice to hit the person) work in my games, which substantially buff a Vampire's survivability. The fact that blood is an easy commodity to replace while Rage and Gnosis, Quintessence and Faith are not, only adds to this.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27252-hades","name":"Hades","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"110"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-05T19:20:36-07:00","id":1483201,"title":"","content":"I'm working on a CoD chronicle with the potential for multiple crossovers and I'm getting a headache.<br /> <br /> Considering those books were ostensibly designed for crossovers and the WoD books were NOT, the headache potential there doesn't bear thinking about.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3201,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3201-father-enoch","user":"Father Enoch","date":". 06-05-2022, 10:23 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3201-father-enoch","name":"Father Enoch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3201_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"285"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-06T04:54:36-07:00","id":1483209,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Father Enoch</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1483135-cross-overs-in-revised-v20?p=1483201#post1483201\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm working on a CoD chronicle with the potential for multiple crossovers and I'm getting a headache.<br /> <br /> Considering those books were ostensibly designed for crossovers and the WoD books were NOT, the headache potential there doesn't bear thinking about.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> They were designed for crossovers meaning that they have pretty much the same basic system with no permutations between dice rolls and such, the actual splats rules are completely different and again not balanced against each other, that being said vampires are actually pretty damn usefull due to their social powers and the fact that they are tanks in requiem but otherwise they are still possibly the weakest and most vulnerable among the splats in sheer power level and unlike Masquerade, elders are not that much better.<br /> <br /> If you are running a crossover, do yourself a favor and either ban mages from the game or make sure you have mature players because awakening mages are even more powerful than ascension and the risk of stealing the spotlight from other players or flatout derailing the chronicle is ever present and I'm saying this as an ST who is running a Geist game with a mage in the party...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27142-newb95","name":"Newb95","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"502"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-06T05:22:04-07:00","id":1483214,"title":"","content":"Never done a mixed PC group, but the other game lines sort of make a show sometimes. NPCs of other splats very rarely make a direct appearance, but their settings do. The power levels don't worry me much, because they're not going to be overshadowing the vampires, a VtM game is about the vampires. They're mostly there for flavour.<br /> <br /> Sometimes you see something weird, like your coeterie meets up at a fast food joint and you notice for the first time that there's a pretty noticable scent of human blood in the kitchen. &quot;What the fuck is wrong with that guy's aura??&quot; You may casually drink off some stranger in an alley and spend the rest of the evening wandering around fairy land. Sometimes werewolves go on a rampage at the company where your ghoul was working. You may observe a bunch of rats wandering around in a suit of human skin, or a death cult that appears to be worshipping somthing called a &quot;Neverborn&quot;. The Elders usually call this &quot;not our division,&quot; don't worry about it.<br /> <br /> Wraith predominates in influence for me, due to Necromancy. If you're playing Giovanni, expect the Underworld to at least be background noise even if you're not dealing with it yourself. Users of advanced Auspex, Dur-An-Ki and Koldunic sorcery can expect some degree spirits and Umbra shenanigans, though I've rarely had cause to bring them in. There are rare banes that can afflict vampires and become a problem for the community. Changelings have their love of political nonsense and their own dealings with the undead, particularly the unseelie who are drawn to vampire's &quot;dark glamour&quot; and the nobles lusting after their own lost immortality, so I can occasionally use them. They also have personal conflicts with the Ravnos that can crop up. Both Wraith and Changeling largely turn up as favour swapping. They're still niche and seldom happen though.<br /> <br /> Fera and mages are too rare, and typically hostile in the former's case, to really make an appearance. Also because I haven't actually played them and have concerns about potential power discrepancies. However kinfolk may make an appearance, and mages should be careful about the stuff they leave lying around. I haven't looked into Mummy, but I might for a Setite game. Demon I don't mind, but have never used. Hunter is an obvious one for crossover, though again I haven't used it. Recent events have me reconsidering that.<br /> <br /> Having vampires aware that the world is bigger than it seems and that there are other things going bump in the night, and frankly, they are just as bad if not worse than you, has worked great for me. Also they have a lot in common with those guys in a way. Blah blah, politics, blah blah, death, blah blah, apocalypse, blah blah, out of touch old people ordering me around.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><sup><i>Prone to hyperbole</i></sup>","edited":{"userid":26836,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26836-rhywbeth","user":"Rhywbeth","date":". 06-06-2022, 09:13 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26836-rhywbeth","name":"Rhywbeth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26836_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"377"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-06T07:57:53-07:00","id":1483221,"title":"","content":"I'm the going to be mutant in the room that actually Loves crossover games.<br /> <br /> The best way to go about it from my perspective has always been to treat each splat like an assigned role. Werewolves are physical combat experts, Vampires are the &quot;face&quot; equiped for mental and social combat, changeling are specialty-expert and non-linear problem solvers, wraiths are the best at stealth, recon, and information gathering, and Mages are NPC ONLY if they show up.<br /> <br /> People don't need to stick to their role 100%(we're not playing d&amp;d after all), but gravitating toward it and giving each role equal spotlight keeps players from being overshadowes. Playing a straight combat game with an ahroun get of fenris and a brujah on the same team will often leave the brujah feeling useless.<br /> <br /> You'll need to make a few quick fixes for various rules conflicts. For Example: when dealing with splats missing humanity and virtue scores various vampire powers need to be decided on an individual basis whether they're contested vs a subsyitute, are rolled against a difficulty instead, or Auto-succeed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6383-prometheas","name":"Prometheas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-06T11:03:33-07:00","id":1483233,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Newb95</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1483135-cross-overs-in-revised-v20?p=1483209#post1483209\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you are running a crossover, do yourself a favor and either ban mages from the game or make sure you have mature players because awakening mages are even more powerful than ascension and the risk of stealing the spotlight from other players or flatout derailing the chronicle is ever present and I'm saying this as an ST who is running a Geist game with a mage in the party...</div> </div> </div> </div>I was hoping to just have NPC Mages that the players would run into by accident looking for someone or something else. They weren't actually going to be major characters, just a cameo for a memorable encounter.<br /> <br /> But I get your point.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3201-father-enoch","name":"Father Enoch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3201_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"285"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-06T11:10:44-07:00","id":1483234,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Father Enoch</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1483135-cross-overs-in-revised-v20?p=1483233#post1483233\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I was hoping to just have NPC Mages that the players would run into by accident looking for someone or something else. They weren't actually going to be major characters, just a cameo for a memorable encounter.<br /> <br /> But I get your point.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> If your game is going to be about demons or mummies then mages could still be added and played without risking stealing the spotlight too much (they can still fuck up the chronicle though), if it's with any other splat then keeping them as npcs is the wise choice.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27142-newb95","name":"Newb95","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"502"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-07T11:22:38-07:00","id":1483321,"title":"","content":"At this point if I were to run a crossover game using Rev/20, I would pick one game as the &quot;home&quot; system and use that system's rules for running the other supernatural types, rather than running each type according to its own rules. So it wouldn't be a true crossover game, and a Lupine in a Vampire game wouldn't be the same as a Garou in a Werewolf game because it would be seen through the lens of Vampires.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27061-random-goblin","name":"Random Goblin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27061_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"20"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-08T04:37:08-07:00","id":1483368,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thoth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1483135-cross-overs-in-revised-v20?p=1483170#post1483170\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Though if you want truely game breaking, do a cross over with Exalted since its original concept was the true prehistory setting of WoD. Caine would probably classify as an Abyssal Half Caste locked at Essence 3, which means most vampires are barely essence 1. Now add an Essence 10 exalt into the setting and watch everything go horribly wrong.</div> </div> </div> </div>Okay this has been bothering me for a while, but don't essence 3 exalted only have an average of 20-30 dice before artifacts?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6383-prometheas","name":"Prometheas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-08T05:37:53-07:00","id":1483369,"title":"","content":"I ran an M20/CTD2e crossover on RPOL for a while. It went quite well, actually. There were a lot of complementary themes. I made an oath that let mages see the enchanted world, and there were shared places of magic (nodes/freeholds). They did have different power levels, but it worked out fine. I had to house rule all the Arts to fix the issues from 2e, but it worked out okay. The style was very high urban fantasy -- they went into the Dreaming, where a mad mage was trying to make himself into a True Fae. It was all quite bonkers, but fun.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-08T11:43:02-07:00","id":1483390,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prometheas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1483135-cross-overs-in-revised-v20?p=1483368#post1483368\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Okay this has been bothering me for a while, but don't essence 3 exalted only have an average of 20-30 dice before artifacts?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes but no, as &quot;average Exalted&quot; isn't really a thing. If dedicated to a given profession, activity or way of life, Exalted are typically specced to kill, with a reasonable expectation to have 10 or more dice before Charms (up to double or so after as an effective rating - Solars roll huge amounts of dice, others have different avenues like dice to success swaps or smaller number of auto-successes). If not, it might not even be a Trait or Traits that they have particularly high unless they're Attribute-based Exalted, in which case they will typically have a high minimum because of the demands of being what they are.<br /> <br /> But there are other difficulties that denizens of the WoD might have in fighting some Exalted. Fire and light-conjuring Solar Charms against vampires, for example. Blazing Solar Bolt would be the end of most Setites, and depending on the edition, a Solar might be able to make melee strikes over a much wider area than that with their &quot;sword pressure&quot;. One introduced in the 2e supplement Glories of the Most High, World-Scarring Glory, could take out several city blocks. Ironically, though, Lunars have to wait a lot longer to turn into city-crushing kaijuu than Mokole, who can do that out of the gate in chargen.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-08T12:13:07-07:00","id":1483392,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1483135-cross-overs-in-revised-v20?p=1483390#post1483390\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes but no, as &quot;average Exalted&quot; isn't really a thing. If dedicated to a given profession, activity or way of life, Exalted are typically specced to kill, with a reasonable expectation to have 10 or more dice before Charms (up to double or so after as an effective rating - Solars roll huge amounts of dice, others have different avenues like dice to success swaps or smaller number of auto-successes). If not, it might not even be a Trait or Traits that they have particularly high unless they're Attribute-based Exalted, in which case they will typically have a high minimum because of the demands of being what they are.<br /> <br /> But there are other difficulties that denizens of the WoD might have in fighting some Exalted. Fire and light-conjuring Solar Charms against vampires, for example. Blazing Solar Bolt would be the end of most Setites, and depending on the edition, a Solar might be able to make melee strikes over a much wider area than that with their &quot;sword pressure&quot;. One introduced in the 2e supplement Glories of the Most High, World-Scarring Glory, could take out several city blocks. Ironically, though, Lunars have to wait a lot longer to turn into city-crushing kaijuu than Mokole, who can do that out of the gate in chargen.</div> </div> </div> </div>I probably should have been more specific. I'm not asking &quot;who would win&quot;, the poster I responded to compared vampires to abyssal exalted. So, since they're similar, I was asking about that.<br /> <br /> I'm more curious about how the abyssals dicepools and abilities measure at different essence levels on average. By &quot;average&quot; I don't mean lore average( which their wouldn't be because exalts are rare in lore), I'm talking about mechanical average based on how options for building a character are broken down.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6383-prometheas","name":"Prometheas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-08T16:13:05-07:00","id":1483414,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prometheas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1483135-cross-overs-in-revised-v20?p=1483392#post1483392\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I probably should have been more specific. I'm not asking &quot;who would win&quot;, the poster I responded to compared vampires to abyssal exalted. So, since they're similar, I was asking about that.<br /> <br /> I'm more curious about how the abyssals dicepools and abilities measure at different essence levels on average. By &quot;average&quot; I don't mean lore average( which their wouldn't be because exalts are rare in lore), I'm talking about mechanical average based on how options for building a character are broken down.</div> </div> </div> </div>Dice pools are almost completely independent of Essence until you get into Essence 6+, at least for first and second edition characters, as the game lazily decided &quot;Essence 6+ means that you can get Traits at 6+ when they normally capped out at 5, not including Virtues&quot;. At this point, specialist dice pools are about Essence x 2, plus three additional dice worth of specialties for a narrower range of rolls - which, in a very cheesy manner, often ended up as &quot;my favorite weapon type + 3&quot;. There were oblique hints of &quot;cap-breaker&quot; effects for Attributes and Abilities in 1e, and 2e kind of added some, but they mostly facilitate getting higher Ability and Essence Charms at a lower rating for said Traits, at least for Abyssals and Solars, so as to not break the math further.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-08T16:55:25-07:00","id":1483422,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1483135-cross-overs-in-revised-v20?p=1483414#post1483414\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Dice pools are almost completely independent of Essence until you get into Essence 6+, at least for first and second edition characters, as the game lazily decided &quot;Essence 6+ means that you can get Traits at 6+ when they normally capped out at 5, not including Virtues&quot;. At this point, specialist dice pools are about Essence x 2, plus three additional dice worth of specialties for a narrower range of rolls - which, in a very cheesy manner, often ended up as &quot;my favorite weapon type + 3&quot;. There were oblique hints of &quot;cap-breaker&quot; effects for Attributes and Abilities in 1e, and 2e kind of added some, but they mostly facilitate getting higher Ability and Essence Charms at a lower rating for said Traits, at least for Abyssals and Solars, so as to not break the math further.</div> </div> </div> </div>What about with charms like exigencies/masteries/etc? I'm not very learned about exalted, but I've heard that exalt have a number of ways to boost their dicepools that I thought were keyed off essence?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6383-prometheas","name":"Prometheas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-08T17:20:24-07:00","id":1483423,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prometheas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1483135-cross-overs-in-revised-v20?p=1483422#post1483422\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What about with charms like exigencies/masteries/etc? I'm not very learned about exalted, but I've heard that exalt have a number of ways to boost their dicepools that I thought were keyed off essence?</div> </div> </div> </div>The charms that boost those dice/success pools, or lower difficulty have a minimum essence rating to be able to purchase them, but not every exalt purchases their charms in the same order. A better way to think of it is Essence is sort of like Generation, a Generation 6 vampire can potentially have access to powerful abilities, but their Generation tells you nothing about what disciplines they have, which would be Clan.<br /> <br /> Essence sort of equals Generation<br /> Exalt type and Caste sort of equal Clan<br /> Terrestrial sorcery (essence 3) sort of equals rank 6+ Thaumaturgy<br /> Manse equals broken games and a traumatized ST <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/727-thoth","name":"Thoth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar727_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1689"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-09T18:11:15-07:00","id":1483539,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prometheas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1483135-cross-overs-in-revised-v20?p=1483422#post1483422\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> What about with charms like exigencies/masteries/etc? I'm not very learned about exalted, but I've heard that exalt have a number of ways to boost their dicepools that I thought were keyed off essence?</div> </div> </div> </div>The Exigency is the 3e process by which the Unconquered Sun lets lesser deities create Exalted, known as Exigents. It doesn't have much to do with this conversation, other than that some of those Exalted might get really weird.<br /> <br /> As for dice pools depending on Essence, well, that's some vocabulary confusion. Essence, the Trait, is a measure of spiritual cultivation. Essence also refers to the cosmic building block of the setting, but when Exalted are using it they're spending motes, a definite quantity like Blood Points, Rage, Gnosis, or Chi, to do something, and the dice-adding Charms generally add one die per mote spent (three motes dedicated to get one die or bonus dot to something for an entire scene, for the &quot;booster&quot; Charms that last longer), and how many you can bank at any given time also depends on Essence, the Trait. There's also a Charm that can expand that capacity (ten motes per purchase), with a caveat for accessing or filling the pool; these were first added in 1e Abyssals, who had what were originally terms Bloodthirst motes. Guess how they had to recharge that pool.<br /> <br /> (It's entirely possible for Celestial Exalted like Solars or Abyssals to walk around with pools that are 40 or 50 motes total at the low end. The expansion Charms can take this over 100 even for those who haven't gotten Essence 6+ yet.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-10T09:13:17-07:00","id":1483608,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thoth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1483135-cross-overs-in-revised-v20?p=1483423#post1483423\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The charms that boost those dice/success pools, or lower difficulty have a minimum essence rating to be able to purchase them, but not every exalt purchases their charms in the same order. A better way to think of it is Essence is sort of like Generation, a Generation 6 vampire can potentially have access to powerful abilities, but their Generation tells you nothing about what disciplines they have, which would be Clan.<br /> <br /> Essence sort of equals Generation<br /> Exalt type and Caste sort of equal Clan<br /> Terrestrial sorcery (essence 3) sort of equals rank 6+ Thaumaturgy<br /> Manse equals broken games and a traumatized ST <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1483135-cross-overs-in-revised-v20?p=1483539#post1483539\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Exigency is the 3e process by which the Unconquered Sun lets lesser deities create Exalted, known as Exigents. It doesn't have much to do with this conversation, other than that some of those Exalted might get really weird.<br /> <br /> As for dice pools depending on Essence, well, that's some vocabulary confusion. Essence, the Trait, is a measure of spiritual cultivation. Essence also refers to the cosmic building block of the setting, but when Exalted are using it they're spending motes, a definite quantity like Blood Points, Rage, Gnosis, or Chi, to do something, and the dice-adding Charms generally add one die per mote spent (three motes dedicated to get one die or bonus dot to something for an entire scene, for the &quot;booster&quot; Charms that last longer), and how many you can bank at any given time also depends on Essence, the Trait. There's also a Charm that can expand that capacity (ten motes per purchase), with a caveat for accessing or filling the pool; these were first added in 1e Abyssals, who had what were originally terms Bloodthirst motes. Guess how they had to recharge that pool.<br /> <br /> (It's entirely possible for Celestial Exalted like Solars or Abyssals to walk around with pools that are 40 or 50 motes total at the low end. The expansion Charms can take this over 100 even for those who haven't gotten Essence 6+ yet.)</div> </div> </div> </div>Okay, so why would Caine be considered an Essence 3 Abyssal, rather than an essence 5 or 10? Everything You've told me so far makes them seem more in line with WoD standard than some kind of uber-craziness.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6383-prometheas","name":"Prometheas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-10T11:15:41-07:00","id":1483618,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vilenecromancer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1483135-cross-overs-in-revised-v20?p=1483171#post1483171\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thoth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1483135-cross-overs-in-revised-v20?p=1483170#post1483170\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oddly enough I don't recall ever seeing a Mage sphere combination for increasing the power of a vampire.</div> </div> </div> </div>Someone make this a thread! We need this specifically!</div> </div> </div> </div>That aint that hard actually. For starters, Entropy 2 to give a few extra successes in anything is always useful. <br /> <br /> Mind 3 can &quot;project&quot; what the Mage can do to himself with Mind 1, there is, Mental Shield to resist domination, mind reading etc, and to improve mental attributes. It can also create multi minds for the vamp to multitask. If the vampire opens himself to it, it's really easy.<br /> <br /> Forces 2 can create an &quot;umbrella&quot; against the annoying sun light, that's a true life saver.<br /> <br /> Other than &quot;common&quot; effects thou, the thing a vamp would benefit the most would be magical trinkets for permanent boons.<br /> <br /> My favorite is the &quot;Vampiric Rose&quot;. Take a considerable amount of the potent Vitae of the bloodsucker - this may take a while and need to let your friend &quot;replenish&quot; several times, but it's well worth it. As everybody knows, Vitae is a powerful Tass. With it you can create SEVERAL trinkets that would be especially attuned to the donor. My favourite one is the &quot;Vampiric Rose&quot; or the &quot;Vampiric Stone&quot;. Basically those are &quot;simple&quot; Periapts, with the special perk of storing &quot;Vitae&quot; instead of &quot;regular&quot; Quint. Gift it to your vamp pal, he now has a supplement battery of Vitae. Life 5 Prime4 or Matter 5 Prime 4 for each, respectfully.<br /> <br /> Now, with Spirit 5, Life 5 and Matter 5, perhaps also Prime 4 or 5, I believe you could also decrease the vamp's generation with the need of sucking elders' souls; that's a massive gift too, albeit a very very hard one multi master level.<br /> <br /> I do somethings that are frowned upon many people... For example &quot;power copying&quot;. That's a house rule of mine, but with Spirit 5 and Mind 3 I let you &quot;copy&quot; powers from others in a very, very hard and complicate ritual. So for example, a Mage could &quot;steal&quot; Spheres from other mages... It could also take disciplines in theory - the knowledge on how to use those, but without Undead bodies they cant use it.<br /> <br /> But with that I would let a Mage copy from disciplines from an Elder to your buddy. The reasoning is that &quot;Disciplines&quot; or &quot;Spheres&quot; or any other are like any other type of knowledge; you CAN &quot;transfer&quot; skills from other people to your mind using mind after all.<br /> <br /> The reason I charge Spirit 5 is because knowledge of Disciplines, Spheres etc aint just a mental pursuit, but a spiritual one too.<br /> <br /> Now, this one may be a little overpowered... Which I would agree, and that's why many people would frown about that idea, but I like it. If you wanna keep it in check somehow, you can always place pattern bleeding (which wouldnt be so hard on vamps if they keep healing with their Vitae), permanent paradox (which again wouldnt be much for a vamp) and/or flaws. Even then, you could add Prime and place those disciplines in an artifact to avoid those nastinesses. Very very powerful option.<br /> <br /> And of course, my Mage can help in several other ways, like keeping the vamp's stuff always clean and sharp with Entropy 3, ripping a hole in Space with Corresp 4 between different world locations so the vamp can quickly escape if needed in also to always move away from day time, creating wards for the vamp's heaven etc etc.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24689-kakost","name":"Kakost","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"586"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-10T11:27:13-07:00","id":1483620,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prometheas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1483135-cross-overs-in-revised-v20?p=1483221#post1483221\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm the going to be mutant in the room that actually Loves crossover games.<br /> <br /> The best way to go about it from my perspective has always been to treat each splat like an assigned role. Werewolves are physical combat experts, Vampires are the &amp;quot;face&amp;quot; equiped for mental and social combat, changeling are specialty-expert and non-linear problem solvers, wraiths are the best at stealth, recon, and information gathering, and Mages are NPC ONLY if they show up.<br /> <br /> People don't need to stick to their role 100%(we're not playing d&amp;d after all), but gravitating toward it and giving each role equal spotlight keeps players from being overshadowes. Playing a straight combat game with an ahroun get of fenris and a brujah on the same team will often leave the brujah feeling useless.<br /> <br /> You'll need to make a few quick fixes for various rules conflicts. For Example: when dealing with splats missing humanity and virtue scores various vampire powers need to be decided on an individual basis whether they're contested vs a subsyitute, are rolled against a difficulty instead, or Auto-succeed.</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually, the Mage CAN be a PC in a cross table. And his role is that of the... Mage! Lol<br /> <br /> Seriously, he plays just like Mages/Clerics from D&amp;D that stay behind doing tricks while using the rest of the party as shields. The Mage in such a table is the Buffer/Debuffer of the game, while the wheres and vamps soak all the hits and the Wraiths and Changes do &quot;rogue stuff&quot;.<br /> <br /> Moreover, the role of the Mage is not to throw fireballs mid combat, but rather to build trinkets in the safety of his lab that increases the overall capabilities of the rest of the party","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24689-kakost","name":"Kakost","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"586"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-10T11:34:17-07:00","id":1483621,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Father Enoch</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1483135-cross-overs-in-revised-v20?p=1483233#post1483233\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I was hoping to just have NPC Mages that the players would run into by accident looking for someone or something else. They weren't actually going to be major characters, just a cameo for a memorable encounter.<br /> <br /> But I get your point.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, do give your players the chance to befriend the Mages. Alliances between Mages and Vamps are powerful ones - vamps can bring social connections, resources and political clout to bear, while the Mages have all the cool toys.<br /> <br /> The vamps could finance a Mage Chantry and use their political connections away from prying eyes, while the Mages can bring an endless bag of tricks to the table. In combat, vamps could smash their enemies, and Mages could bring new capabilities to the vamps that their bloodsucking rivals would never expect.<br /> <br /> If your players are smart during that encounter, give them a chance to roleplay and perhaps unite. For example, make the big baddy of the vamps be in league with the big baddy of the mages - justifying both of you bumping togheter - and perhaps they can work togheter this time, and maybe become pals later.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24689-kakost","name":"Kakost","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"586"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-10T12:09:31-07:00","id":1483631,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kakost</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1483135-cross-overs-in-revised-v20?p=1483620#post1483620\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Actually, the Mage CAN be a PC in a cross table. And his role is that of the... Mage! Lol<br /> <br /> Seriously, he plays just like Mages/Clerics from D&amp;D that stay behind doing tricks while using the rest of the party as shields. The Mage in such a table is the Buffer/Debuffer of the game, while the wheres and vamps soak all the hits and the Wraiths and Changes do &quot;rogue stuff&quot;.<br /> <br /> Moreover, the role of the Mage is not to throw fireballs mid combat, but rather to build trinkets in the safety of his lab that increases the overall capabilities of the rest of the party</div> </div> </div> </div>That role could be just as easily filled in by Sorcerers and Mummies though.<br /> <br /> The issue I have with mages is the fact that they are Orders of Magnitude more powerful than a D&amp;D wizard in the hands of a creative player. A mage doesn't need meat shields the way a D&amp;D wizard does, a properly built starting mage is either as powerful as most vampire ancillae one vs one or doesn't need to be in the same room to kill them.<br /> <br /> That isn't even power-gaming things, that's just how mage plays. The central theme of mage is essentially going &quot;Yes, you can do X, but Should you?&quot; and dealing with the aftermath of how a mages actions affect themselves and others when they let hubris get in the way of wisdom.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6383-prometheas","name":"Prometheas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-10T12:36:56-07:00","id":1483637,"title":"","content":"One of the problems regarding balance stems more from a single fact that affects mostly PCs, that is that unlike in Vampire, mage players and werewolves aren't the &quot; lamest and least powerful creature among their kind who's barely superior to the average human&quot;. So, it's a simple problem that has indeed a greater importance than it may seem at first glance and I've known several players who didn't feel like playing vampire for this exact reason. Vampire PCs are expected to start the game way too &quot;lame&quot; for their kind, as one friend once put it to me &quot;You can't even FEEL like a TRUE vampire with 3 dots in disciplines and everybody around you and their mother is more powerful than you&quot; and I'd say he's not really wrong. The perception is that the PCs in vampire are so vulnerable and weak that it's really hard not to feel damned while you can't see the sun anymore and still you can barely overcome a normal human in overal strength. Just imagine if Mage PC's started with only 2-3 dots in spheres and/or you had mostly only access to perception powers, it sure would feel different, but instead Mages start with 6 dots in spheres, they're probably not that impressive for their kind, but still they can definitely FEEL like real mages, the same thing is true for Werewolves, to start they begin with the powers associated to werewolves from legends, (I'd say even much more so, as werewolves in WoD are clearly superior to the general werewolf from legends, as WoD is the only universe I know where werewolves are the &quot;best fighters in the world&quot;) they can change form at will, etc, so they don't really depend on Gifts, Gifts for werewolves are just pluses, now imagine if the only feature starting werewolves PCs had was being vulnerable to silver and then they'd be closer to what the average PC feels when starting a vampire game lol<br /> <br /> Unfortunately, vampire core books didn't change the starting points in later editions and didn't offer much alternative, like expressing in the books that you could make PCs start with more than 3 dots in disciplines, etc. I know many people who dare not attempt things that aren't mentioned in the books, especially inexperienced STs. So, the inexperienced ST is going to bring these discrepant views of these beings into one world and certainly vampire PCs are going to be the least interesting/powerful by far. That's why I usually advise people wanting crossovers to make it so with elder's rules, this way you avoid making your vampire players simple support actors in the story. Of course, one could argue that if you make an overly social game, that's going to make the vampires shrine much more than the others, but it's usually very simple to turn a social situation/scene into a combat one with a few gestures, so to speak lol","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12348,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12348-herr-meister","user":"Herr Meister","date":". 06-10-2022, 03:59 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12348-herr-meister","name":"Herr Meister","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12348_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-10T12:44:52-07:00","id":1483639,"title":"","content":"Has anyone tried a Vampire Chronicle where players can start with 6 ranks in Disciplines? Or did they just give them 15-25 bonus experience to start? <br /> <br /> If you did let a Vampire PC start with 6 ranks, how many would you restrict to in Clan Disciplines?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3201-father-enoch","name":"Father Enoch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3201_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"285"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-10T13:04:23-07:00","id":1483640,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Father Enoch</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1483135-cross-overs-in-revised-v20?p=1483639#post1483639\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Has anyone tried a Vampire Chronicle where players can start with 6 ranks in Disciplines? Or did they just give them 15-25 bonus experience to start?<br /> <br /> If you did let a Vampire PC start with 6 ranks, how many would you restrict to in Clan Disciplines?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Throughout my years of experience as ST, I've tried many different combinations. Like 6 dots in disciplines, with at least half into clan disciplines, sometimes I give more bonus experience tied with a good story that I give points depending on how well-developed it is, etc.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12348-herr-meister","name":"Herr Meister","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12348_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-10T16:21:05-07:00","id":1483656,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prometheas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1483135-cross-overs-in-revised-v20?p=1483608#post1483608\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Okay, so why would Caine be considered an Essence 3 Abyssal, rather than an essence 5 or 10? Everything You've told me so far makes them seem more in line with WoD standard than some kind of uber-craziness.</div> </div> </div> </div>Exalted can create something called a &quot;half-caste&quot; which is an offspring that shares a limited level of that exalts power and charm set. They are capped at Essence 3 and can't go further without gaining full exaltation, but those are limited in number. There are only about 100 or so Abyssal Exaltations at any given time. Abyssals were modelled to be the prehistory Cainite splat.<br /> <br /> The interesting thing is that Exalted had rules for bloodlines of power, so things like a half caste clan or beastman clan were possible and could breed true without further interaction with the exalt progenitor. The essence 3 cap lines up with the limited disciplines the most powerful elder vampires have.<br /> <br /> Essence 3 charms sit about where discipline 6+ disciplines are, Essence 6+ charms allow for things like reshaping reality, creating new worlds, reworking the laws of physics, etc. In some ways high essence charms make Mage spheres look limited in power, depending on which exalt type we are talking about.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/727-thoth","name":"Thoth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar727_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1689"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-10T16:37:02-07:00","id":1483659,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Father Enoch</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1483135-cross-overs-in-revised-v20?p=1483639#post1483639\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Has anyone tried a Vampire Chronicle where players can start with 6 ranks in Disciplines? Or did they just give them 15-25 bonus experience to start?<br /> <br /> If you did let a Vampire PC start with 6 ranks, how many would you restrict to in Clan Disciplines?</div> </div> </div> </div>I have done this a couple of times. One was a very long game and the other was a more limited type.<br /> <br /> The long game was set in prehistory, everyone was a 5th generation Follower of Set. Standard character generation rules, except they started with 11 discipline dots rather than 3 and could go above five dots from the start without spending extra points. We played from prehistory all the way through to post apocalypse. With that much game time the characters were more or less max statted in everything by the end. This game played out more like an exalted abyssal game than anything else.<br /> <br /> The shorter game was modern nights, the coterie was just a group of normal human friends who went camping, they got attacked by some roving sabbat who were hungry and bored. The humans managed to fight off the vampires which impressed a passing gangrel elder who then killed the sabbat and embraced the humans on a whim. Once she was done giving the &quot;welcome to the club&quot; speech, she went on her way leaving the childer to fend for themselves. The coterie had several adventures but eventually they got their bloodline checked, turns out their sire was the Gangrel antediluvian, and all of them have been running around with fortitude 9 as a hidden stat the entire time, with the normal 3 discipline dots randomly put into animalism and protean. As the ST I had been rolling the soak rolls and passing the lack of damage as really bad luck attack rolls on the part of the enemies.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/727-thoth","name":"Thoth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar727_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1689"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-11T17:23:48-07:00","id":1483765,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thoth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1483135-cross-overs-in-revised-v20?p=1483656#post1483656\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Exalted can create something called a &quot;half-caste&quot; which is an offspring that shares a limited level of that exalts power and charm set. They are capped at Essence 3 and can't go further without gaining full exaltation, but those are limited in number. There are only about 100 or so Abyssal Exaltations at any given time. Abyssals were modelled to be the prehistory Cainite splat.</div> </div> </div> </div>We don't use that term for Chosen-Blooded anymore.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The interesting thing is that Exalted had rules for bloodlines of power, so things like a half caste clan or beastman clan were possible and could breed true without further interaction with the exalt progenitor. The essence 3 cap lines up with the limited disciplines the most powerful elder vampires have.<br /> <br /> Essence 3 charms sit about where discipline 6+ disciplines are, Essence 6+ charms allow for things like reshaping reality, creating new worlds, reworking the laws of physics, etc. In some ways high essence charms make Mage spheres look limited in power, depending on which exalt type we are talking about. </div> </div> </div>Essence 3+ Charms specifically reshape reality for Solars and Solar-alikes where reality is already unsettled and soft, typically in the Wyld or Labyrinth, the latter of which is a capability that Abyssals only got in 2e, with the 1e &quot;equivalent&quot; instead being &quot;watch me turn this area of chaos into a blighted wasteland and only a blighted wasteland, btw fuck the Fair Folk&quot;. Infernals got some limited capacity to rework settled Creation in 2e, but they're overwritten and sat as the New Cool Thing for a bit too long.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-13T02:24:46-07:00","id":1483854,"title":"","content":"I ran 4 year campaign all players were vampires (as they always) are<br /> I used mages and nerfed them rarely<br /> Used Garou by Garou rules and it was fun<br /> Used Scion alot and it mixed pretty well just balanced action wise all actions were calculated and turns per vampire rules.<br /> Used Red Death triology and made lameth.<br /> <br /> Demons were nerfed heavy but still made great danger<br /> Campaign was based on Gehena and general metaplot of 2.0 mixed with V20.<br /> <br /> They used up to 6 dots on mentor using merits so they could learn other clan disciplines (one of party mentors was mage and vampire depending on reality which was replaced by real mentor later and used as one of villains for rest of the campaign)<br /> <br /> Campaign started in 96(2014 IRL) and they ve reached 2003 and Tehnocracy kicking ass out of any supernatural trying to own a tank or similar stuff.<br /> On start ther were 4 players and they would sometimes branch out in 2x 2 groups Separate sessions untill they come agains as whole group<br /> Party was Nosferatu(investigator),Caitiff (Hammerhead),Caitiff - Modern samurai /blood mage hacker and Ventrue with Ancient ghoul (background gift) <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4185-ragnor","name":"Ragnor","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"22"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}